  "title": "Countably n-rectifiable sets have approximate tangent spaces a.e. (Simon Ch. 3, Theorem 1.6 '⇒')",
  "statement": "Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let M ⊆ ℝ^P be a Borel, countably n-rectifiable set with H^n(M ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ ℝ^P (H^n = μHE[n]). Then for H^n-a.e. w ∈ M (that is, for μHE[n].restrict M-a.e. w) there is a linear subspace Q of ℝ^P such that Q is the approximate tangent space of M at w (HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M w Q).",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P n : ℕ) (M : Set (Euclid P)), MeasurableSet M → CountablyRectifiable n M → (∀ K : Set (Euclid P), IsCompact K → μHE[n] (M ∩ K) ≠ ∞) → ∀ᵐ w ∂(μHE[n].restrict M), ∃ Q : Submodule ℝ (Euclid P), HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M w Q",
  "lean_name": "codim1_rdo_rectifiable_ae_approxTangent",
